focas-proto
===========

focas-proto is an independent implementation of the FANUC FOCAS/Ethernet wire protocol. It is
not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by FANUC CORPORATION and contains no FANUC code or
library. FANUC and FOCAS are trademarks of FANUC CORPORATION.

Credits
-------

pyfanuc  (https://github.com/diohpix/pyfanuc)  by diohpix  -  Unlicense (public domain)
    The wire protocol was reverse-engineered there. The framing, function numbers, request
    arguments, payload layouts, scaled-number format and the sample packets used by the codec
    tests come from its pyfanuc.py, protocol.txt, README.md, sample_multipacket.md and
    sample_with_error.md.

pyfocas  (https://pypi.org/project/pyfocas/) 0.1.1  -  MIT
    Copyright (c) 2026 Moritz Breurather, Rene Schwaiger
    The macro write function (01 a8) and the byte-level description of scaled numbers were
    checked against it. No pyfocas code is copied; only the function number and request layout
    of write_macro are taken from it. pyfocas in turn credits pyfanuc.

FANUC FOCAS documentation (as published by inventcom.net)
    Field names and the meaning of statinfo, sysinfo, alarm and axis-position values follow it.
    No text or code from it is included.

Origin
------

The code was written for the voltrus project (crate mt-focas, same author), developed further in opex-flow, and is
vendored back here from there (see VENDORED). In this repository it is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later like the rest of
the workspace.
